\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{A block sum can cross the principal-angle cut}
\date{2026-11-27}

\p{Take the uniform scalar field of \ref{fdip-015W} with flux #{10} on an #{8\times 8} torus. The angle of each plaquette is #{5\pi /16}. Multiply fine edge transports in pairs to pass to period #{4} in each direction. Each coarse cell has phase #{\ue^{5\pi\ui /4}} by cancellation of its #{4} small plaquette boundaries, hence principal angle #{-3\pi /4}. The coarse flux is #{16(-3\pi /4)/(2\pi)=-6}. The sum inside a cell exceeds the principal-angle range, although every fine plaquette has its angle inside that range.}
